## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are current authority. Vimla is messenger-first with one backend for Web and future Desktop/Mobile.

Composer behavior is a communication-surface concern. New Group/Channel/Direct/AI thread composition must share typed semantics where appropriate without assuming all surfaces have identical permissions or encryption. Mentions/content never grant authority.

# Messaging / AI composer

Model selection belongs only inside ordinary AI Composer. Never render page-level AUTO/PRO controls.

Root: Auto > / PRO. Auto submenu: Minimum / Medium / Maximum. PRO opens a separate model picker with search/capability filters. Concrete models appear only in PRO picker.

AI Composer includes a dedicated `◆ @Vimla` control. It must be designed for structured mention insertion, not regex side effects from arbitrary text.

Direct/project human composer has no model selector by default. Dedicated Vimla operator conversation has no model selector at all.

Phase 6.1 may implement presentation/readiness for structured mentions but must not implement Phase 7 operator execution backend.
